# Repo workflow

- Don't commit or push unless the user asks. Don't change git config.
- Commit as the user, through environment variables: `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME` and `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME` = `Tanzim Nasir`,
  `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL` and `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL` = `tanzim.nasir@eliteintegrityservices.com`.
  Git is `C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe`; remote `origin`, branch `main`.
- Never stage `README.md`; it stays modified and uncommitted. Stage files by name, not `git add -A`.
- Write the commit message to a UTF-8 file and use `git commit -F`.
- Scratch scripts go in `C:\Temp` and are deleted afterwards, one file at a time; never delete `C:\Temp` recursively.
- The app loads the code when it starts: after a change, the user has to close and reopen "Elite SW Auto".
